Revision history for Perl extension Unpack-SevenZip

{{$NEXT}}

    - 7z is run without a shell: archive names and switches may contain
      any characters (quotes, spaces, leading '-')
    - array references passed to info and extract are no longer modified
    - corrupted files are detected with 7-Zip >= 15 ("ERROR: CRC Failed : path")
    - nothing is printed to STDOUT; unexpected output is reported by carp,
      files which were not extracted are returned as the third value of
      extract (and reported by carp with verbose => 1)
    - info: no empty entries for trailing warnings/errors sections, entries
      of unknown size (e.g. bzip2) get the rest of the output, entries
      without a name get the archive name without extension
    - output truncated in the middle of a file is reported as corrupted
    - stdin of 7z is closed right away so it never waits for input
    - the exit code of 7z is stored in last_exit_code
    - new dies nicely when the 7z binary does not exist
    - tests are skipped when 7z is not installed, GitHub Actions instead
      of Travis, author e-mail changed

0.01 2015-03-11T12:00:01Z

    - original version

